{
  "title": "LearnHouse \u2014 edtech (1,642\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: LearnHouse\nDomain: edtech | Scale: medium | Stars: 1,642\nProblem: LearnHouse is an open-source learning management platform that enables educators and organizations to create, manage, and deliver world-class educational content with modern features like AI-powered tools, code execution, real-time collaboration, and analytics.\nTarget users: Educators and instructors, Educational institutions, Organizations and enterprises, Course creators, Learning administrators\nCore features: Course creation and management with block-based Notion-like editor; AI-powered interactive elements, simulations, and diagrams (Playgrounds); Code execution with auto-grading in 30+ languages; Real-time collaborative whiteboards (Boards); Student assignments tracking and submission management; Analytics and engagement tracking dashboard; Community discussions and forums; Podcast content support and certificate generation\nIntegrations: Google Gemini AI, Stripe (payments), OAuth providers (SSO), Docker (deployment), PostgreSQL (database), Redis (caching/sessions)\nTech stack: Next.js, React, TypeScript, TailwindCSS, Radix UI, Tiptap, CodeMirror, Yjs + FastAPI, Python + PostgreSQL, Redis + Docker, self-hostable with CLI\nKey libraries: Next.js, React, TypeScript, TailwindCSS, Radix UI, Tiptap, Yjs, CodeMirror, FastAPI, Stripe, Google Gemini\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Polyglot full-stack approach: TypeScript/React frontend with Python FastAPI backend enables specialized tooling for each domain (UI frameworks vs. ML/AI integration)\n- Real-time collaboration is core: Yjs integration for whiteboards and collaborative features indicates strong emphasis on synchronous learning experiences\n- AI-first design: Context-aware AI components throughout (code execution, content generation, playgrounds) show AI as a platform capability rather than an add-on\n- Self-hosting and developer experience prioritized: Custom CLI tool for setup, deployment, and management reduces friction for institutional adoption and self-hosting",
